# reading 2 of berkeley-principles-4.md by claude-opus-5-5
atom	borrowed_terms	men are used to speak of the nature and operations of the mind in terms borrowed from sensible ideas
atom	controversies	men are engaged in controversies and mistakes with regard to the nature and operations of the mind
atom	will_motion	the will is termed the motion of the soul
atom	ball_belief	there is a belief that the mind of man is as a ball in motion, impelled and determined by the objects of sense as necessarily as a ball by the stroke of a racket
atom	moral_errors	endless scruples and errors of dangerous consequence arise in morality
atom	reflect	philosophers retire into themselves and attentively consider their own meaning
atom	cleared	these errors are cleared, and truth appears plain, uniform and consistent
